meta {
  name: List Appointments
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/portal/appointments
  body: none
  auth: none
}

script:post-response {
  // The soonest appointment, used by Cancel Appointment and Reschedule Appointment.
  const first = res.body?.data?.appointments?.[0]?.id;
  if (first) bru.setVar("portalAppointmentId", first);
}

docs {
  Requires the server to run with `ENABLE_SELF_SERVE=true` ("Mis citas" is off by default: every
  /portal path answers 404) and a `portal_session` cookie. No login issues that cookie now that the
  codes are gone, so this request only works against a session minted for a future login.

  Needs the `portal_session` cookie. Returns `{ appointments, requests, consentRequired }`: the session
  patient's upcoming active appointments (at most 50, soonest first) once they have accepted the
  current privacy policy, otherwise `{ appointments: [], requests, consentRequired: true }` with the same shape
  whether or not the email belongs to a patient.

  `requests` are the session email's live PENDING booking requests (approval mode), listed even when
  `consentRequired` is true because they belong to the verified email itself.

  Each appointment carries `canCancel` and `canReschedule`, computed on the server: cancel for any
  upcoming active appointment; reschedule only for online bookings whose type and location are still
  bookable online, while the provider takes bookings in auto-confirm mode.
}
